From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] win32u, user32, comctl32: Keyboard cues (6541)

A new profile now hides access-key underlines and focus rectangles until
the keyboard is used, as Windows does by default; "Underline access keys"
(SPI_SETKEYBOARDCUES) still shows them always. Wine had always shown them
(UserPreferencesMask 0x30) and had no UI state at all, so programs that
draw their own menus by that setting (iTunes) showed "File_ Edit_".

Windows keep a UI state (UISF_HIDEACCEL, UISF_HIDEFOCUS). A child takes
its parent's; a top-level window hides both unless the last input was a
key. DefWindowProc answers WM_QUERYUISTATE, passes WM_CHANGEUISTATE up
to the top-level window, which sends WM_UPDATEUISTATE down to every
child when the state changes. Alt or F10 shows the access keys; Tab and
the arrow keys in a dialog show the focus rectangle and the access keys.
DrawText honours DT_HIDEPREFIX and DT_PREFIXONLY. Buttons and labels
(classic and common controls 6) and menus draw by the state, which they
read without a message (NtUserCallHwnd_GetUIState), as Windows' controls
send none while painting; a menu opened with the keyboard underlines,
one opened with the mouse does not.

Only the default changes: a profile that already has UserPreferencesMask
keeps it.
